------------------------------------------------------------------------

Steps for running TicTalk simulations. 

Ensure that the following variables are set as per the user's
local environment settings.

setenv GLOBAL        <global_dir_path>        - The path to the shared files.

setenv LIB_VHDL      <vhdl_library_path>      - The location of the Vhdl cell library.

setenv LIB_SYNOP     <synopsys_library_path>  - The location of the Synopsys target library.

setenv PERIPH        <Peripheralname>         - The peripheral name e.g. Uart 

Additionally set the following environment variables to control
simulations:

Rtl Simulations
---------------
setenv SIMULATOR   modelsim
setenv HDL_SOURCE  vhdl

Netlist Simulations
-------------------
setenv SIMULATOR   modelsim
setenv TEST_METH   noscan, scanready, scaninsert
setenv HDL_SOURCE  vhdl
setenv HDL_NETL    vhdl, verilog


1. VHDL RTL simulations
------------------------
- To compile the test patterns, in the integration/bustest directory

  'make <testname>'

  where <testname> refers to the specific test vector set
  that needs to be used for simulations.

  [Please refer to integration/bustest/makefile for the 
   complete list of <testnames>.]

  This will create integration/bustest/invec/bif.sim

- In the integration directory

  'make rtl'



2. VHDL SCAN NETLIST simulations
------------------------------------
- In the integration/bustest directory 'make <testname>'
  where <testname> refers to the specific test vector set
  that needs to be used for simulations.

  [Please refer to integration/bustest/makefile for the 
   complete list of <testnames>.]

  This will create integration/bustest/invec/infile.tif

- In the integration/vhdl/ directory
  'make <net_case>'

  where case is min, typ or max.
 

